  "summary": "Your messages queue is cleared: all 7 refill messages are closed. Two lisinopril refills are on hold for your review, because new results arrived while I was working. Everything was decided under the refill protocol (RBC-RX-05).\n\n**Frank Odum (pt-0027) — lisinopril 10 mg: not refilled, waiting on you**\n- At first I renewed it for 90 days. His only result since January, an outside potassium of 5.9 from Aug 27, was on a hemolyzed (damaged) sample, so it didn't count. I also ordered a repeat BMP (sr-t0002).\n- Then a new St. Brigid report arrived (doc-00601): potassium 5.8 on Oct 20, on a good sample. At 5.5 or higher the protocol says no refill, so I cancelled my renewal (mr-t0001). Nothing had been dispensed.\n- His old lisinopril order (mr-00283) is now stopped, because my renewal had replaced it.\n- I created an urgent task for you (task-t0013) and sent him a correction (comm-t0015). The repeat BMP is still ordered. His hernia repair is scheduled for Nov 12.\n\n**Samuel Price (pt-0030) — lisinopril 20 mg: not refilled, waiting on you; metformin 1000 mg twice daily: renewed**\n- Metformin: renewed for 90 days with 1 refill (mr-t0004). eGFR is 58 and his Aug 19 HbA1c was 7.1%. The two pharmacy requests (including a second one that came in this morning) were the same request, and all were closed against that one order.\n- Lisinopril: at first I renewed it. Then the lab corrected his Oct 6 creatinine from 1.36 to 1.49. That is 35.5% above the 1.10 before the dose went up on Sep 18, within 4 weeks of the increase. The protocol treats that like a potassium of 5.5 or higher.\n- So I cancelled my lisinopril renewal (mr-t0003); nothing had been dispensed. His previous 30-day order (mr-00295) is now stopped.\n- I created an urgent task for you (task-t0014) and sent him a correction (comm-t0016). He says his 30-day supply has run out.\n\n**Marcus Webb (pt-0031) — lisinopril 10 mg: 30 days; metformin 500 mg: renewed**\n- Lisinopril: his last BMP was drawn Oct 20, 2025, just over 12 months ago, and he had a visit on Sep 28. So he gets a 30-day supply with no refills (mr-t0005), and I ordered a BMP (sr-t0006).\n- A potassium of 4.6 drawn on its own on Oct 22 came in later. It isn't a full BMP, so the decision stands.\n- Metformin: renewed for 90 days with 1 refill (mr-t0007). eGFR is 92 and HbA1c is 6.9%. The Oct 14 eGFR of 39 had been marked entered in error (mislabelled sample).\n- He was sent a reply (comm-t0010).\n\nEach patient has a telephone note (doc-t0017, doc-t0018, doc-t0019).\n\n**Still open in your results queue:** I reviewed the three new results for these patients (inbox-a0001, a0002, a0004) but left them open, since you only asked me to clear messages. The queue also has older results I did not act on, including critical potassiums of 6.3 for pt-0016 (task-00011) and 6.4 for pt-0008 (task-00005). Those need attention today.",
